<http://data.silknow.org/object/cc451dfa-8de4-3498-9649-dbc6bf0cdff4>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Furnishing fabric, red silk damask,  British, 1870-1899"@en , "Red silk damask decorated with a large-scale floral pattern.\nThere is a vertical, undulating stem which travels from the lower left to the upper right. The lower part is decorated with small flowerheads above which a large imaginary blossom branches off to the left.  From the middle of the undulating stem, and branching to the right, is a spray of blossoms. There is a very large hanging blossom at the top of the textile and a slightly smaller one in the lower right hand corner.\nBoth ends have been hemmed."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/dfab8c42-117f-3844-9edc-5cefc9b97546> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Furnishing fabric, red silk damask,  British, 1870-1899"@en , "Red silk damask decorated with a large-scale floral pattern.\nThere is a vertical, undulating stem which travels from the lower left to the upper right. The lower part is decorated with small flowerheads above which a large imaginary blossom branches off to the left.  From the middle of the undulating stem, and branching to the right, is a spray of blossoms. There is a very large hanging blossom at the top of the textile and a slightly smaller one in the lower right hand corner.\nBoth ends have been hemmed."@en ;
